{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1161047-combine-the-might-of-a-warstrider-with-the-lunar-power-of-heart-s-blood","id":1161047,"title":"Combine the might of a Warstrider with the Lunar power of Heart's Blood","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-20T19:20:12-08:00","id":1161047,"title":"Combine the might of a Warstrider with the Lunar power of Heart's Blood","content":"Not a suit of armor, like Unison, that merely continues to cover a Lunar as she transforms into a tyrant lizard.<br /> <br /> Not a Warstrider with a set alternative shape, like Escaflowne.<br /> <br /> Rather, a Warstrider so specialized for shapeshifting that even a non-Lunar pilot can use it to devour a fallen behemoth and then urge the Warstrider to transform into a mechanical mirror-image of the conquered beast.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lunars can already assume forms of Legendary Size with the Towering Beast Form Charm, or whatever the Charm will be named in Third Edition. But these forms will not allow Devastating attacks, and will likely be balanced with expensive committed mote costs, Willpower costs, and possibly reduced mote respiration, or even a negative mote drain per turn.<br /> <br /> But what if a Warstrider could be designed to <i>merge</i> with a Lunar? To serve as a <i>magnifier</i> for Towering Beast Form, with its crafted strength and considerable upkeep costs off-setting the Lunar's personal strain.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I picture looks superficially similar to the Walking Devil Tower, being humanoid with claws and teeth. (These and other &quot;natural&quot; weapons the Warstrider can sport might count as barehanded for Brawl Charms and Lunar Charms, at the writer's discretion.)<br /> <br /> When a pilot uses this machine-monster to eat her fallen foes, the Warstrider absorbs their Heart's Blood for its own use, and also shares it with the pilot so that she doesn't have to get out and taste them personally. I see this as being done through an initially-unlocked Evocation very much like Eat the Heart of God.<br /> <br /> <br /> Non-Lunars would need to learn a special Evocation that represents this Warstrider shapeshifting into the form of the Legendary Sized creature they ate. This Evocation might require repurchasing for each new form, depending on how the writer wants to balance it. A following Resonant-locked Evocation might allow a Solar the ability to eat creatures smaller than Legendary Size in order to make the Warstrider become Legendary Sized versions of those creatures. Another Resonant-only Evocation after that might allow the pilot to access one of the special Behemoths that the Warstrider is famed for having eaten under the control of previous pilots, at the <i>Storyteller's</i> discretion.<br /> <br /> While shapeshifted, the warstrider is still a machine rather than a biological creature, so it retains its invulnerability to poisons and diseases. It also retains Warstrider-specific advantages like Devastating attacks. If the stolen form's original creature had any Charms, only Eclipse-OK Charms become available to the pilot, barring any Solar or Lunar Charms that would grant access to other Charms from the original creature.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lunars will need only one Evocation at most to shapeshift the Warstrider into any permissible form, though it will probably require they know Towering Beast Form (or whatever Charm allows them to assume the forms of creatures with Legendary Size). Since I imagine that Towering Beast Form will require hefty committed mote costs, a steady mote-cost upkeep per turn, and various other balancing factors, this Warstrider serves as a way for a Lunar to bypass those limitations by borrowing the Warstrider's existing size and power. While also enjoying Warstrider-specific advantages like Devastating attacks.<br /> <br /> With their own Heart's Blood Libraries, Lunars also wouldn't be limited to forms contained within the Warstrider, if they know Mountainous Spirit Expression (or whatever Charm allows them to become a Legendary Sized version of a smaller creature).<br /> <br /> <br /> For flavor, I can see three possible cockpits:<br /> <br /> (1) The cockpit is filled with a buoyant fluid that suspends the pilot safely in place, with gentle, tendon-like control-strands that connect to her body. These respond easily, without the resistance of other Warstriders (for Lunars, the Strength requirements are already met with Towering Beast Form's Strength minimum). On the other hand, pilots stuck with human bodies can find it challenging to control inhuman forms without familiarizing themselves with the proper contortions (which may require a Specialty). Lunars who fuel the transformation with their own shapeshifting don't have this problem; the cockpit is designed like it is in order to accommodate virtually any creature's form. A Lunar who assumes a Legendary Sized form while in the cockpit is actually forced to remain roughly human-sized as their shapeshifting/growing power is focused through the Warstrider.<br /> <br /> (2) The pilot simply merges with the Warstrider when it shapeshifts, in order to bypass awkwardness in regards to Solars trying to move like birds or squamus octopus-like things.<br /> <br /> (3) No physical controls, just psychic ones. The pilot sits in the cockpit without personally shapeshifting, even if Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T11:24:08-08:00","id":1161927,"title":"","content":"So, which cockpit idea do people like more?<br /> <br /> I wouldn't bother asking, but apparently some people care enough to keep glancing at this thread, at least. So I wonder if maybe they have an opinion about which funky driver's seat this monster has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T12:15:57-08:00","id":1161935,"title":"","content":"I would go with the first, with an idea that non-shapeshifters get a certain sense of puppetry of the altered body indirectly, rather than direct correspondence of movements. That might possibly be helped if behemoths are not <i>too</i> varied in forms.<br /> <br /> \u200bHow large do you envisage the Heart's Blood library of the thing being able to become?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T13:10:22-08:00","id":1161947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1161047-combine-the-might-of-a-warstrider-with-the-lunar-power-of-heart-s-blood?p=1161935#post1161935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would go with the first, with an idea that non-shapeshifters get a certain sense of puppetry of the altered body indirectly, rather than direct correspondence of movements.</div> </div> </div> </div>If non-shapeshifting pilots don't experience any problems, then there's no reason for a shapeshifter to personally change forms when the Warstrider does. Plus, a Lunar assuming a baby T-Rex form to fit within the cockpit when the warstrider turns into Mecha-Rex is... silly.<br /> <br /> The Evangelion womb-cockpit idea can stay, but the nerve-tendrils would need to connect to the pilot for the purpose of reading her mind rather than serving as control-straps to yank on to physically puppet the mecha.<br /> <br /> So a Lunar temporarily shares her Heart's Blood with the mecha to facilitate its transformations, but she doesn't change her own form while in its cockpit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bHow large do you envisage the Heart's Blood library of the thing being able to become? </div> </div> </div>Initially, a non-Lunar pilot would be restricted to things she personally hunted. That limits the library to things like yeddim, elephants, ox dragons, siege lizards, tyrant lizards, river dragons, orcas, whales, giant squid, and other mega fauna. Along with any Fair Folk beasties, behemoths, or spirits(gods or elementals or demons) that assumed a form of Legendary Size to fight the warstrider.<br /> <br /> The prey must have Legendary Size, because the Warstrider will not shrink below that weight class.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unlocking anything that the pilot hasn't personally defeated, but that the Warstrider has eaten in the past, would probably require special conditions. Like, &quot;You can't learn the Evocation for assuming the form of Kalameet, the One-Eyed Black Dragon of Disaster, until you have used the Warstrider to consume (or your personal Heart's Blood library contains) a number of weaker but similar creatures as determined by your Storyteller&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that might be a Resonant effect, or else forbidden to anyone who is Dissonant with moonsilver.<br /> <br /> As for how large the Warstrider's personal collection of behemoths and other novel beasts are, that's mostly up to its legend and the storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T14:15:51-08:00","id":1161965,"title":"","content":"When I suggested the first one, I meant the need for a Specialty and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T14:58:19-08:00","id":1161976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1161047-combine-the-might-of-a-warstrider-with-the-lunar-power-of-heart-s-blood?p=1161965#post1161965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I suggested the first one, I meant the need for a Specialty and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Come to think of it, needing a Specialty after buying an Evocation JUST for a specific form would be stupid and petty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}